    "author": "ZPLC Team",
    "created": "2024-12-24",
    "modified": "2026-10-09",
    "iecStandard": "IEC 61131-3",
    "notes": [
      "Larson scanner with contacts, coils and one TON:",
      "1. Rung 1 is a self-resetting tick: TimerInst runs while Tick is FALSE and its Q is Tick, TRUE for one scan.",
      "2. P0..P5 are a one-hot ring of six positions (D0 D1 D2 D3 D2 D1). On a tick each position takes its",
      "   predecessor; between ticks it holds its value (the second path of each shift rung).",
      "3. The shift runs from P5 down to P1 so each rung still sees the old value below it; P5 is saved in Carry",
      "   first and P0 takes it last.",
      "4. D0 = P0, D1 = P1 or P5, D2 = P2 or P4, D3 = P3.",
      "With a 10 ms task the first step is at 150 ms and then one step every 170 ms (150 ms + 2 scans)."
    ]
  }
